<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Baker Hughes reduced.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Baker Hughes reduced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brown Brothers Harriman &amp; Co Michael LaMotte cut his long-term rating for oil services company Baker Hughes Inc Thursday to market perform from outperform.</p>
<p>-- He kept his short-term hold rating for the company.</p>
<p>-- The downgrade was caused by Baker Hughes' &quot;lack of visible pricing power, potential loss of management credibility and better relative opportunity elsewhere,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Shares in Baker Hughes were up 7/16 to 42-7/16 in heavy trade.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
